<title>INDIA: Bombay sugar markets shut in protest over tax hike.</title>
<headline>Bombay sugar markets shut in protest over tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombay sugar markets were shut on Wednesday as traders observed a strike to protest a government tax hike, Shantilal Dedhia, secretary of Bombay Sugar Merchant's Association said.</p>
<p>The market will also remain closed on Thursday for the same reason, he said. It will reopen for trading on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
